# Neo Envelope parameters (docs/specs/neo-patch.md §3). The order is permanent: songs and presets store values by position.
# Regenerate: python3 tools/gen-machine-params.py Machines/NeoEnvelope
namespace NeoBuzz.Envelope
class NeoEnvelopeMachine
summary An envelope that moves other machines' parameters, up to 8 targets each with its own depth, polarity, range and curve. Note mode: an ADSR started by the notes of a chosen machine (and track) or by its Gate switch. Follower mode: follows the level of a chosen machine's output, with attack and release and a threshold (ducking, envelope-driven filters). Use it for a filter that opens on every note, a pad that ducks under the kick, an effect that opens with the drums.

group Shape
Mode      "Mode"        0 1 0    enum Note Follower            | Note: an ADSR started by notes. Follower: follows the level of a machine's output
    id mode
    how Chooses an ADSR started by notes (Note) or a follower that tracks the level of a machine's output (Follower).
    sound Note mode opens and closes with each note; follower mode rises and falls with the loudness of the machine it listens to.
Attack    "Attack"      0 1000 313 time 0.001 5                | Note: time to rise to the top. Follower: how fast it follows a rise in level
    id attack
    how Sets how long the rise takes, from 1 ms to 5 s; in Follower mode, how quickly it follows a louder signal.
    sound Short is a snap, long is a slow swell.
Decay     "Decay"       0 1000 500 time 0.001 5                | Note mode: time to fall from the top to Sustain
    id decay
    how Sets how long the fall from the top to the Sustain level takes (Note mode).
    sound Short decays make a pluck; long ones let the movement hang on.
Sustain   "Sustain"     0 1000 700 pct                         | Note mode: the level held while the note is held
    id sustain
    how Sets the level held while the note stays down (Note mode), from 0 to 100 %.
    sound At 100 % the movement stays at the top; at 0 % it is a single pluck with no hold.
Release   "Release"     0 1000 500 time 0.001 5                | Note mode: time to fall to nothing after the note ends. Follower: how fast it follows a fall in level
    id release
    how Sets how long the fall to nothing takes after the note ends; in Follower mode, how quickly it follows a quieter signal.
    sound Short releases cut the movement off; long ones let it trail away.
Threshold "Threshold"   0 600 0  lin -60 0 dB 0                | Follower: levels at or under this are zero; 0 dB is the top
    id threshold
    how Sets the level, from -60 to 0 dB, below which the follower reads zero.
    sound A higher threshold ignores quiet bleed, so the follower only reacts to the loud hits.
Curve     "Curve"       0 1000 500 bip                         | Bends the output: negative eases out (fast start), positive eases in (slow start)
    id curve
    how Bends the output from -100 % (fast start, eases out) to +100 % (slow start, eases in).
    sound Negative curves make the movement jump then settle; positive curves hold back then rush.

group Control
Gate      "Gate"        0 1 0    switch                        | A manual gate in Note mode: on starts the envelope, off releases it (patterns can write it)
    id gate
    how Starts the envelope when switched on and releases it when switched off, with no notes needed (Note mode).
    sound A pattern writing this switch triggers the envelope on its own steps.
Glide     "Write glide" 0 1000 408 time 0.001 1                | Time a target takes to cross its whole range: no write moves further than this allows
    id glide
    how Limits how fast a target may move: it takes at least this long to cross its whole range.
    sound A short glide keeps fast modulation clean; a long one smooths and slows it.
